-- Penelope import (bourbon.penelope: shop.penelopebourbon.com, the brand's own Shopify store — penelopebourbon.com itself rarely states a number), applied 2026-09-24 via the Supabase MCP. No hand steps.
-- Two fixes made along the way, both in shared code, verified against all 19 previously-applied sources:
--   catalog/bourbon/normalize.py:age() treated a bare range with no lead verb ("4 - 6 Years Old") as a specific number (matching its last digit) instead of a display label; it now matches the same as "aged 4 to 6 years".
--   The module's own blend-vs-single-whiskey check counted the word "and" in a finish description ("honey barrels and then Amburana barrels") as a second whiskey type; fixed to count actual type keywords (Straight Bourbon / Straight Rye / Single Malt / Light Whiskey).
-- Five ready-to-pour cocktail SKUs on the same store, and the site's own /nutritional-information/ page (a single static Four Grain entry, not a full per-SKU table), were not usable and are not crawled.

